WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.467
-Finally, you guys,
spring is here.

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:04.400
Okay? Are you feeling this?
The weather...

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:10.934
The weather is warming up.
The flowers are in full bloom,

00:00:10.934 --> 00:00:12.734
which inspired me
to write a song

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:14.968
with one of our good friends,
Andy Samberg.

00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:16.534
Here, take a look.

00:00:16.534 --> 00:00:18.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.968 --> 00:00:24.667
♪♪

00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:25.801
♪ I'm a plant dad ♪

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:27.067
♪ I love plants ♪

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:28.767
♪ Water them, sun them,
do a little dance ♪

00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:29.801
-♪ I'm a plant dad ♪

00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:31.000
♪ Plants love me ♪

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.000
♪ Dig them, raise them,
one, two, three ♪

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.000
-♪ Go into the garden,
get on my knees ♪

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.868
♪ Give a little drink
to my bonsai trees ♪

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:38.868
-♪ I've got my pot,
I've got my seeds ♪

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:41.000
♪ I give little kisses
to the itty-bitty leaves ♪

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.868
-♪ Fill a whole hothouse,
that's my dream ♪

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:44.868
♪ I like to go green,
if you know what I mean ♪

00:00:44.868 --> 00:00:45.701
-♪ I know what you mean ♪

00:00:45.701 --> 00:00:46.868
♪ I love plants, too ♪

00:00:46.868 --> 00:00:48.734
♪ My wife is leaving me
for another man ♪

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:50.701
-♪ I'm a plant dad,
I love plants ♪

00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:52.667
♪ Water them, sun them,
do a little dance ♪

00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:53.767
-♪ I'm a plant dad ♪

00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:55.000
♪ Plants love me ♪

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.968
♪ Dig them, raise them,
one, two, three ♪

00:00:56.968 --> 00:00:58.734
-♪ Succulents don't need
that much water ♪

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:01.000
♪ And they like to live
where it's much hotter ♪

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.801
-♪ Caring for plants,
it gives me structure ♪

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:05.067
♪ She had an affair
with her yoga instructor ♪

00:01:05.067 --> 00:01:06.968
-♪ I can't get enough
of my orchids ♪

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:08.968
-♪ She and Braden want
to have more kids ♪

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:11.000
-♪ Sprouts are short,
plants are long ♪

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.934
-♪ I'm afraid of Braden,
he seems strong ♪

00:01:12.934 --> 00:01:14.834
-♪ One plant D-A-D I be ♪

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:16.534
-♪ My kids already
call him daddy ♪

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:17.534
-♪ So -- ♪
-♪ Couples therapy ♪

00:01:17.534 --> 00:01:18.901
♪ Then went badly ♪

00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:21.000
♪ She said I tried to coop
her up like Bradley ♪

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.000
♪ Then she also said
she slept with Bradley ♪

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.767
♪ Then she also said
she slept with Chad Lee ♪

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:26.701
♪ I said, even so,
I love her madly ♪

00:01:26.701 --> 00:01:28.868
♪ Then the therapist
called me a simp ♪

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:30.901
♪ She said
take some time to self-reflect ♪

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:32.701
♪ And, quote unquote,
find some self-respect ♪

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:34.901
♪ But instead I went straight
to my former house ♪

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:36.868
♪ In search of my soon-to-be
former spouse ♪

00:01:36.868 --> 00:01:38.634
♪ I dropped to my knees
and begged her please ♪

00:01:38.634 --> 00:01:40.734
♪ To be in a throuple with me ♪

00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:42.300
♪ They politely passed
after thinking it through ♪

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.601
♪ They said,
We're open to a throuple ♪

00:01:43.601 --> 00:01:45.300
♪ Just not with you,
which hurt ♪

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.667
♪ So I walked down the block ♪

00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:48.667
♪ I came back later,
but they changed the lock ♪

00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:50.834
♪ So I burrowed a hole
underneath the house ♪

00:01:50.834 --> 00:01:52.767
♪ And lay there all night,
quiet as a mouse ♪

00:01:52.767 --> 00:01:55.434
♪ Listening to them bone ♪

00:01:55.434 --> 00:01:56.801
-Should --
Should I, like, go?

00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:58.701
-♪ As I lay there,
buried like a plant ♪

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:00.901
♪ I can hear them grunt,
I can hear the pant ♪

00:02:00.901 --> 00:02:02.267
♪ The sweat drips
down through the floorboards ♪

00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:04.334
♪ Onto my forehead ♪
♪ I can hear four words ♪

00:02:04.334 --> 00:02:07.033
♪ They are worthless, worthless,
worthless, worthless ♪

00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:09.000
♪ Why am I here?
What is my purpose? ♪

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.033
♪ Smile on my face,
but my laugh is mirthless ♪

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:13.067
♪ I just have to be down
where the dirt is ♪

00:02:13.067 --> 00:02:14.067
♪♪

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:16.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.734 --> 00:02:18.801
-♪ I'm a plant dad,
I love plants ♪

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:20.701
♪ Water them, sun them,
do a little dance ♪

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:22.834
♪ I'm a plant dad,
plants love me ♪

00:02:22.834 --> 00:02:25.267
♪ Every plant I ever raised
[bleep] died ♪

00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:31.100
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:33.334
-The one and only Andy Samberg
right there!

00:02:33.334 --> 00:02:36.133
Check out his new show,
"Digman!"

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:38.634
airing Wednesdays at 10:30
on Comedy Central.

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:39.801
We love you, Andy.

